The desk's [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) described a known
month-first parser problem and assumed the entire merged ticket needed one fix.
The export instead shows separate mechanisms within `sched-prod`.

This review uses the export dated 4 October, not a live ticket-system feed.
Keep incoming desk updates separate from this snapshot and re-run the views
before changing the counts.

## Engineering update: different closure reasons

The [course desk update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) reports
that #4471 closed on **5 October 2026**, after the export:

- **Parser: FIXED**, with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Its
  engineering issue is closed as **completed**.
- **Hint: WON'T FIX**, because the **booking-v3 form was retired**. Its
  engineering issue is closed as **not planned**, not as a delivered fix.

This supersedes the earlier snapshot's statement that a fix was merely queued.
The engineering team reported the parser fix; this repository neither
implements it nor independently verifies production behavior. Retirement
explains the hint issue's closure without claiming that the hint was corrected.
Neither resolution changes how the original reports are counted.

## Separate engineering issues

- [Shared parser reads month first](https://github.com/mikimik01/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
  A day-first tenant's app/email dates, and dates through booking-v2, reach the
  shared month-first parser. An intended 7 April can become 4 July.
- [Booking-v3 hint disagrees with the form's parser](https://github.com/mikimik01/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
  For day-first tenants, the form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while reading the tenant's
  order. Following that hint for 6 August can produce 8 June. Correcting the
  shared parser does not correct this hint.

## Counts derived from the export

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

`uniqueById` removes overlapping export rows before the view selects reports
merged into the source ticket. `tenantOf` resolves the tenant directory, and
`causeOf` uses the tenant's date order, form version, and report channel.
`dayFirst` asks `Intl.DateTimeFormat` for the locale's date-part order rather
than maintaining a guessed list of European locales.

The intake-tag column is deliberately separate from the cause. Intake guessed
from the reporter's browser; its labels disagree in both directions. The table
counts by cause, not by those labels. A booking-v3 tenant's app/email reports
are not automatically form-hint reports.

## Evidence and uncertainty

`R-41200` is a parser example: harbour.dental uses `en-GB` and booking-v2, and
the app report describes 7 April becoming 4 July. `R-41205` also takes the
parser path despite an `en-US` browser and an intake tag of `hint`: the actual
tenant is morrow.tax, using `fr-FR` and booking-v2.

`R-41241` is a hint example: alder.physio uses `de-DE` and booking-v3, and the
report came through the form. `R-41230` and `R-41251` take the same form-hint
path for copper.studio and pale.harbour even though intake called them `parser`.

<Callout>
The desk's one-day observations are unresolved, not proof of a timezone cause.
The count footnote shows where the supplied classifier files them. Retain the
reports and investigate the mismatch instead of silently excluding them or
claiming a confirmed additional bug.
</Callout>

The flagged IDs are `R-41202`, `R-41209`, `R-41236`, `R-41344`, and `R-41620`.
Their bodies include a one-day shift, an invite apparently preceding a booking,
and different weekdays reported in Lisbon and Toronto. Those observations do
not establish a common mechanism. The parser issue explicitly retains them
for follow-up under the supplied classification.

## Received is not merged

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports were arriving before July. A later batch of merges records a desk action,
not the start of the defect or a sudden burst of newly received reports. Read
both series and their dates before making a claim about incident onset.

## The rule that replaces subject-only merging

Use the [current triage procedure](/kb/triage/dedupe) and
[decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause). Confirm the same product and
cause before merging. A matching subject does not make the parser and form hint
one issue; different subjects do not make reports of the same parser bug
different issues. Unknown tenant context is not a match.

Decision 0001 remains unchanged as an accepted historical record. A `known`
ticket status and an old review date do not override the current evidence.
Likewise, a closed status alone does not distinguish a fix from a retired
feature: retain the desk's reason for each closure.

